{"internal_reasoning": "I have sufficient B and G chips for nearly any path, but lack R chips for the direct minimal path—only missing 1 R. The other player has many R chips but no B, while I have many B and no R. If I can get an R covered for my (0,2) to (1,2) or (0,1) to (1,1) step, I can take the shortest path and finish with more chips. My best path uses (0,0)->(0,1)[B]->(1,1)[R]->(1,2)[B]->(2,2)[G]->(2,3)[B]->(3,3)[B] but I'm missing the R for (1,1), so I want the other player to cover (1,1) for me. In exchange, perhaps I cover one B at a crucial spot for them (if they need, e.g., (2,3) or (2,2) or (3,2)). I should propose this minimal, mutually beneficial exchange.", "external_message": "You have many R chips and I have many B chips. To take my shortest path and maximize my remaining chips, I need one R covered at (1,1) (the tile south of (0,1)). In exchange, I can cover a single B chip for you at a tile you choose. For a fair exchange: 

(1,1): You give me an R 
You choose one tile where you want a B covered, and I will cover it for you (please specify the tile)."}
